          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            that behaves likes the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
          %p
            A boolean domain object internal to a topos is an object that behaves in that topos like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Bool}
            does in Set.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_a_topos_or_cartesian_closed_category In a topos or cartesian closed category
          %p
            A
            %strong boolean domain object
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            (or any
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is
