          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_an_initial_object As an initial object
          %p
            The boolean domain object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            in the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-pointed+object"} bi-pointed object
          %h3#coproducts Coproducts
          %p
            The boolean domain object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+coproduct"} disjoint coproduct
            of the terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            with itself.
          %p
            … (One should be able to define binary
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            functor and the boolean domain object, as dependent sums exist in topoi and cartesian closed categories.)
          %h3#products Products
          %p
            … (Same thing as above but with binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            and
            = succeed "s.)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
          %h3#subobject_classifier Subobject classifier
          %p
            A topos with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            that is also a boolean domain object is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+topos"} two-valued topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of such a topos is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+logic"} two-valued logic
          %h3#type_theory Type theory
          %p
            Boolean domain objects are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            in type theory. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive property
            of the boolean domain type, case analysis or if/else expressions, corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initiality
            of the boolean domain object in the subcategory of triples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, t:1\rightarrow A, f:1\rightarrow A)
            representing
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-pointed+object"} bi-pointed object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            corresponds to the initiality of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            in the subcategory of triples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, q:1\rightarrow A, f:A\rightarrow A)
            representing infinite sequences.
